# Accepted findings from `trivy config`, each a deliberate trade-off for a $0 deployment.

# The k3s node pulls images, OS updates and Helm charts and calls AWS APIs and PayPal; there is
# no NAT gateway or egress proxy to narrow it to (that would be ~$32/month)
AWS-0104

# S3 buckets use SSE-S3 (AES-256) instead of a customer-managed KMS key, which costs $1/month
# per key; the buckets are private, versioned and block all public access
AWS-0132

# spring-webmvc 6.2.x: fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9, which needs the Spring Boot 4
# migration; no 6.2 release has the fix. The expiry makes the build fail again on that date so
# the exception is revisited rather than forgotten.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
